WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.901
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show!"

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.701
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:08.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.400
Well, guys,
everybody is talking about this.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.234
Last night, CBS aired
a two-hour special

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:16.000
called "Adele: One Night Only."

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.434
Yep. The special brought in
10 million viewers.

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:22.200
CBS heard and was like, "Sorry.
We meant '100 Nights Only.'

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.901
Sorry."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:27.033
Yep, more people watched
Adele's special than the Oscars.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.400
Although more people
are watching their

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.200
Ring doorbell cameras
than the Oscars.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:33.400
Yep, that's right.
In the special,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.234
Adele opened up about
the pain of her divorce.

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:38.334
It was tough to sit through.
Right after, I had to re-watch

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:39.968
"Squid Game"
just to lighten my mood.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:43.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:46.334
That's right.
Adele said that she knew

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.701
she needed to end her marriage

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:50.300
when she was doing
a magazine quiz.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.868
[ Audience "Awws" ]
Even crazier, it was Buzzfeed's

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.801
"Which character from
'Hocus Pocus' are you?"

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:58.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.667
You can tell everyone at CBS
was excited about Adele.

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.767
Check out the beginning
of "60 Minutes" last night.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.000
[ Watch ticking ]

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.534
-♪ Go easy on me, baby ♪

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.868
-Oh.
[ Watch ticking ]

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That was at the beginning?

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:15.767
I didn't see the beginning.
-Wow!

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:16.834
-Let's get to some news.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.601
Today, President Biden
finally signed

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:22.133
his $1.2 trillion
infrastructure bill.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.567
Yep. Now we all get one day
to celebrate before America

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.534
turns into one
giant construction site.

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:27.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:29.801
Of course, by the time
we actually fix all the roads,

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.267
everyone will be riding
in drones.

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:34.467
I'm excited about the bill.
I mean, soon we can stop

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.000
making the sign of the cross
before driving over

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.033
the George Washington Bridge.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:41.567
"All right, I love you guys.
You know that, right?"

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.133
Some more political news.
Today, Beto O'Rourke released

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:47.901
a video officially launching his
campaign for governor of Texas.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.267
Watch this.

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.734
-I'm running for governor,
and I want to tell you why.

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:54.901
I want you on the team,
and I want to win this with you

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:58.467
and for you and for all
the people of Texas.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:01.400
-Your aunt was like,
"Until 'Bridgerton' comes back,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.367
this is as good as it gets."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.100
Can we see Beto again?

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.601
Forget governor.
He looks like he should be

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:08.601
selling homemade honey
at a farmers market.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:11.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:13.934
"Two -- Two for 10 bucks?"

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:15.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.634
Some business news.
I heard that Costco just

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:20.334
warned its customers
of a potential data breach

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:24.100
after they found a credit-card
skimmer in one of their stores.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:27.000
Or, as the thief put it, "I just
bought some identities in bulk."

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:31.334
Yeah, it's hard to spot
credit-card fraud at a Costco,

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.501
'cause every purchase seems
like a strange purchase.

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:37.000
It's like, "What's that?
$5,000 on cheeseballs?"

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.200
"That actually was me.
Sorry.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.501
Okay, yeah, that was me.
Sorry."

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:44.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:46.801
"My kids are playing in
one of the cheeseball containers

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:49.267
right now. It's awesome."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:51.801
Hey, I saw that Gucci
is releasing a special edition

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.968
Xbox that comes
with two controllers

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:56.334
and a branded suitcase
for $10,000.

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:58.133
Check this thing out.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.467
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.501
-That's right. Great.
Right after I just spent

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:03.267
12 grand
on a Chanel PlayStation.

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:04.300
-Oh.
-You know?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.501
[ Laughter ]
-Seriously, for 10 grand,

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:09.501
a Gucci Xbox should come
with Adam Driver and Lady Gaga.

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:13.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:16.367
Well, get this -- a new poll
found that, due to rising costs,

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:19.400
nearly half of Americans
will soon cancel at least

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.033
one of their
streaming subscriptions.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:23.534
You know as soon as
you cancel Netflix,

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.100
you're gonna hear your neighbor
scream through the wall,

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.734
"What the hell?"
You go...

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:27.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:29.634
"I was almost done
with 'Squid Game'!"

00:03:29.634 --> 00:03:32.067
"Sorry."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:33.634
Well, this is very exciting.
This weekend,

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:36.667
the Rockefeller Center Christmas
tree arrived in New York City.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:43.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
Right outside.

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:44.868
And I know what everyone
is thinking.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.567
Yes, the tree
has been vaccinated.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:47.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:50.033
What's crazy is, this is
actually last year's tree.

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:52.167
It just got here now
'cause of supply-chain issues.

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.100
And finally, border officials
in the U.K.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.000
found $44 million
worth of cocaine

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.801
hidden in a shipment
of onion rings.

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:04.234
Yep.
$44 million in onion rings,

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:05.801
plus another million
in the one french fry

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.300
that was in there by mistake.

